{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1457274-random-niche-question-theory-are-vampires-the-creation-of-a-philosophers-stone","id":1457274,"title":"Random niche question/theory; are vampires the creation of a philosophers stone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-20T09:22:42-07:00","id":1457274,"title":"Random niche question/theory; are vampires the creation of a philosophers stone?","content":"So I randomly thought of V5's resonance and how vampires are now alchemic in nature and then KotE and then I started skimming stuff on alchemy and had ridiculous ideas that I'm going to inflict on this forum to pour them out of my head so they stop distracting me.<br /> <br /> The goals of alchemy is the refinement of the human body and soul to perfection and the <i>Magnum Opus </i>- the creation of the Philosopher's Stone, which essentially covers regenerative properties like the healing of diease and injury, bypassing the laws of science, and immortality. Y'know. Vampire stuff.<br /> It also creates the elixir of life which passes portions the property to anyone who imbibes it. Sort of like a ghoul. Or, more relevant, like creating a new vampire.<br /> <br /> <i>Magnum opus</i> has four stages, assuming I wrapped my head around them correctly, they are destruction/decay, reconstruction/purification, enlightenment and, uh, the consolidation of all three prior stages(?)<br /> The end result would be all the advantages of the vampire, with none of the weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Under this model I would suggest that a vampire is in the process of the magnum opus, specifically stage two (<i>albedo</i>).<i> &quot;The albedo is the second stage of alchemy. In this process, the subject is divided into two opposing principles to be later coagulated to form a unity of opposites.&quot;</i> Like... the split between the human cognitive thoughts and the base instinct of the inhuman beast? Maybe?<br /> <br /> Stage One is <i>nigredo</i>, the death and deconstruction of the base human. The result splits it into the human higher cognition and the vampiric instincts of the beast, which need to be unified by subjugation or reconciliation via humanity/paths. One assumes the following stage is somehow getting to an invisible eleventh dot on the path... or maybe it's generation and you're meant to (somehow) build your way to 1st gen.<br /> Could be the other way around. Lower generation brings you closer to your beast and/or purifies the base human material, maybe?<br /> <br /> Of course, if this ridiculous theory was right and the Noddists were also right then vampires may be damned to eternal imperfection because <i>somebody</i> murdered all the 2nd generation. (Everyone should join the Sword of Caine for revenge, those ancient assholes ruin everything.)<br /> i suppose this'd mean that Caine is the original philosophers stone and all ghouls and vampires are imbued with the elixir of life from him...<br /> <br /> There's a homebrewed path of enlightenment in this, somewhere. Probably made by a Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-20-2021, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T10:58:13-07:00","id":1457283,"title":"","content":"I love alternate origin myths for the Kindred and I adore this one. Even if it's bunk, the heavy reliance on Renaissance Hermeticism strongly hints at when a vampire might have first thought of it. <br /> <br /> It's therefore already better detailed than the Caine myth - which falls apart not only in the face of several branches of the physical sciences, but also in the face of Judaism still today being a relative newcomer in the long history of human religious beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T12:07:18-07:00","id":1457288,"title":"","content":"I would like to steal this for a Tremere that's pursuing the mythical Golconda (perhaps w/o all the Diablerie business, that seems doomed from the start). The mythic state supposedly allows one to surpass or make amends with the Beast, and parts of the Curse itself. So, it checks. And it sounds like something an uncharacteristically spiritual Tremere could believe. If it's true or not...that's a whole different matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T12:14:39-07:00","id":1457290,"title":"","content":"The idea did not leave me alone.<br /> It occured to me that this would add an explanation to the Antediluvian's behaviour. If the 3rd gen wipes out the 2nd, and in response the 1st generation/Caine removes them/himself utterly from their reach in punishment, the 3rd generation have destroyed their ability to reach perfection. They are beyond human, they are gods in power but they've shot themselves in the foot and can never shed their final curses or acheive the final completion stage of <i>rubedo</i>.<br /> <br /> All of them are searching for a loophole. Cappadocius, unable to diablerise Caine aims a step higher. He will diablerise god. Saulot scours the world for a new path to enlightenment. Haqim devours the unfinished, younger vampires. Perhaps the essence of the stone, spread amongst the thousands will (when collected) be sufficient for the magnum opus. The Eldest has gone a step further and wants to absorb every living thing on the planet.<br /> Other, regular vampires seek out alternative means of raising their generation to diablerie.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;stone&quot; I would imagine that would be what the Assamites call &quot;heart's blood&quot;; the liquid containing the soul that gathers in a vampire's heart, growing more potent and refined with age and experience. It's also the substance that is consumed in diablerie. It also produces a lesser variant of the elixir of life (aka, vitae), transmuted from human blood. The completion of the magnum opus finally refines the heart's blood into a philosopher's stone at the heart of the vampire (which is not, necessarily, a literal stone. Heck, this entire stone process, if true, would probably be a metaphor that explains the enlightenment process)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-20-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T00:00:58-07:00","id":1457319,"title":"","content":"I'm loving this. You should write it up for the ST's Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T12:16:13-07:00","id":1457342,"title":"","content":"he recent DAV20 france by night had something about cainites and alchemy, notably tremeres that compared vampires to an ongoing alchemical process.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's yet translated in english, If not, I'll do later a translation here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 08-21-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T16:19:36-07:00","id":1459704,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, here's the text from DAV20 France by night, translated by your humble servant<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Alchemy and Ca\u00efnites<br /> <br /> This &quot;science&quot; that is said to come from ancient Egypt and transited by Greece and Byzance begins to attract the attention of numerous scholars seeking to accomplish the Great work which will lead to the famous philosopher's stone, a concept still hardly known in this early XIIIth century.<br /> <br /> If numerous fantasies linger around the philosopher's stone which could change lead into gold, it's true power lay in the fact that it may give eternal life. The succession of the four phases of the Great work, ultimate accomplishment of the alchemist after decades of studies, researchs and experimentation, goes through the blackening, the whitening, the yellowing and the reddening. This last step allow the making of the scarlet stone so desired.<br /> <br /> If, for alchemists, these steps of successives transformations are real, some of them, knowledged in the more occult arts, think that the Great work is but a symbolic representation of ca\u00efnite vitae, this deep red liquid which gives life everlasting. This symbolism is found in the myth of the Graal and the blood of Christ, to which are attributed the power to heal all ills and, of course, to give an exceptionnal longevity.<br /> <br /> The mystical crucible in which the transmutations proper to alchemy would be then in reality the human body, transformed in the diverses steps of the Embrace in order to become a ca\u00efnite. In that, the Great work would be a &quot;gift&quot; from God, althought that gift would be in reality a curse.<br /> <br /> The true objective of the rare ca\u00efnites adepts is to succeed in practicing the &quot;alchemical Embrace&quot;, a ritual of transformation so pure that it would clean the blood of the Damned from it's curse while still confering the powers of immortality and might coming with it. Popular amongs some members of clan Tremere, this theory would allow the embrace while conserving the advantages of true magick that the founding Usurpers were robbed of. <br /> <br /> The discovery of such process would allow, according to them, to purify the blood of a vampire by a methodic application of rituals, of the path Potestas Vitae (path of blood) and of solar &quot;calcination, in order to eliminate the impure elements. The vampire would abandon the ranks of the Damned to join those of the immortal mages. Creatures so powerful that they'd have the world within their hand.<br /> <br /> While the majority of the Tremere laugh at these ridiculous theories, who knows what are the actual limits of their blood magic? They can already augment the strenght of their vitae and even break the powerful blood bond, this mystical link born in even the weakest blood and able to erase the will of the most resilient and obstinate beings.<br /> Is the alchemical Embrace truly a fantasy? Could the myth of Golconda be one of the initiatic path toward this secret?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T19:05:54-07:00","id":1459712,"title":"","content":"Two thoughts; first this would be an amazing path to add to the alternate Sabbat from the \u201cTzimisce in charge of the Cam\u201d thread; both in the \u201cyoung eat old\u201d anti-elder sentiment (diablerie as ascension towards the philosopher\u2019s stone) and as a something you could latch onto the idealistic perfection of society that the Brujah always go on about.<br /> <br /> Second, I could see a flipped version of this emerge from the thin-blooded... sure they aren\u2019t gods, but their curses are weakened, they are still superhuman and immortal. One could argue that the ability to actually conceive a child is proof that the purification is not by concentrating the Curse but by pulled the metaphorical gold from the shit that\u2019s been sloughed off in the putrefaction stage and that either the last generation or their semi-immortal offspring (a superhuman with some of the strength but almost none of the weaknesses) represents the culmination of the Great Work and that each successive thinning until it could finally find true synthesis with a mortal human has been a step on that path.<br /> <br /> Particularly in light of thinblood alchemy, and merits like daydrinker, you could have two competing schools of alchemical thought on what the true Great Work is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}